Subject: Cantor SJS Commit Envelope Journal P2 Input Audit

@ [audit_uuid] fb93d660-d5ef-48a6-8e13-b92070486814
@ [canonical_uuid] 27ac629d-a885-49f1-85ca-14c52c2f3b0e

& [ConfirmedInputs]
  + P0 DiffInventory digest covers every changed coordinate and P0 exact coverage requires event-coordinate set equality
  + P0 candidate manifest requires resulting_commit null while committed or published requires an exact commit identity
  + candidate and published forms can independently validate against the same inventory after recomputing their change-set and receipt digests
  + P1 physically acquires the staged inventory but intentionally excludes commit-envelope self-inclusion

& [CycleProof]
  + if the manifest path is in the described inventory then inventory_sha256 depends on raw manifest bytes
  + raw manifest bytes contain inventory_sha256 and change_set_sha256 so exact same-payload construction is recursively self-dependent
  + foreign exclusion cannot solve the cycle because an owned envelope path is not foreign
  + a special ignored self path would break P0's exact bidirectional coverage contract

& [SelectedResolution]
  + time-shift envelope custody by one commit and retain one explicit open tip
  + validate both candidate and published forms plus successor placement as separate immutable evidence

& [RemainingGap]
  + P2 supplied placement is internally verified data and not physical Git tree observation
  + no process mutation operator authorization recovery hook or push broker is selected
